WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.582 --> 00:00:03.862
The agent has written a useful program. To run it,

2
00:00:03.942 --> 00:00:07.222
the application selects a human-approved blueprint and binds the

3
00:00:07.462 --> 00:00:11.062
customer ID from trusted context. An agent can help draft

4
00:00:11.142 --> 00:00:13.542
the blueprint; a human owns its rules.

5
00:00:16.418 --> 00:00:19.707
The application sends code to the authenticated server. It

6
00:00:19.787 --> 00:00:23.307
parses and type-checks supported TypeScript, then compiles it to

7
00:00:23.427 --> 00:00:27.387
WebAssembly. A type error stops the program before it runs.

8
00:00:30.182 --> 00:00:33.542
Inside the server process, the runtime creates an execution

9
00:00:33.622 --> 00:00:37.382
instance and runs main. The program calls its billing package,

10
00:00:37.622 --> 00:00:40.422
which reads a local fixture standing in for a service.

11
00:00:43.382 --> 00:00:46.582
Before returning charges, the package calls a permission check

12
00:00:46.662 --> 00:00:50.102
with the operation and customer ID. Its author placed this

13
00:00:50.182 --> 00:00:52.822
checkpoint; it is not inferred for every function.

14
00:00:55.615 --> 00:00:58.975
The runtime compares the requested ID with the blueprint rule

15
00:00:59.055 --> 00:01:02.575
and the ID the application supplied. A match allows this

16
00:01:02.775 --> 00:01:04.815
lookup; another customer is denied.

17
00:01:07.781 --> 00:01:10.981
The program totals permitted fixture records and returns its

18
00:01:11.221 --> 00:01:15.141
result: two charges, six thousand one hundred and fifty cents.

19
00:01:15.781 --> 00:01:19.781
Compilation checks the program. Runtime permission checks decide

20
00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:23.221
whether the requested operation and customer ID are allowed.
